// mutationSendPrivateUtterance, mutationMovePrivateToGroup,
// mutationMoveGroupToPrivate, and mutationRecordMisrouteFeedback were
// extracted to the product pack
// (the carrier repo's pack mutations file) by Epic 3
// (3.3b-i, memql#1991) along with the v1:cognition:privateUtterance +
// v1:cognition:misrouteFeedback concepts (ids preserved). The two
// "move" mutations touch BOTH privateUtterance (moving) AND utterance
// (staying core) -- in the pack they import utterance via
// `use cognition.concepts.{ utterance }` and the moved concepts locally.

// ---- mutations/v1/cognition/rolloverDailySpace.memql ----

// rolloverDailySpace
// ==================
//
// Inserts the terminal version of a daily space at rollover: the
// dailyspace integration's sweep (memql#1384) passes the full merged
// payload with status flipped to "archived" or "saved" (per the
// owner's preferences.dailySpaceRolloverAction) and active=false.
//
// Mirrors the leaveSpace / updateParticipantStatus
// "caller passes the full updated payload" pattern. A dedicated
// mutation (instead of mutationArchiveSpace / mutationSaveSpace) is
// required because those stamp ownerUserId from actor.userId -- the
// sweep runs under the synthetic system:dailyspaceAutomation actor,
// which must NOT become the space owner. The sweep preserves the
// real ownerUserId in the payload it passes.

